tweets.text:
Bravo Zulu to the crew of U.S. Coast Guard Cutter Tahoma (WMEC-908) for their successful drug offload in Port Everglades, FL, today. Teaming up with our partners at @jiatfs, the crew seized an impressive 9,970 pounds of cocaine. As the nation’s maritime counter-drug leader, the Coast Guard is increasing operations to interdict, seize, and disrupt transshipment of cocaine and other bulk illicit drugs by sea.

Our maritime interdiction efforts play a crucial role in disrupting cartels, combating the flow of illegal narcotics including fentanyl, and protecting American communities from this pressing threat. #USCG #druginterdiction #ValueToNation
@USCGSoutheast @USCGLANTAREA @DHSgov

